#:layer #!pragmatics

^["intent"]{
 ~#goal: "Introduce visible workspace/package seams for v0.3.0 by making the repo a workspace root and adding package-level entrypoint facades before any large-scale physical code moves."
 ~#taste: "layering, clarity, containment"
}

^["stream"]{
 >>[2026-03-20 00:07] observe — the repo currently has only src/{seed,runtime,testing} plus root scripts; package ownership is implied rather than encoded.
 >>[2026-03-20 00:07] observe — scripts and extensions reference src/seed, src/runtime, and scripts/lsp directly, so a full move would create broad churn.
 >>[2026-03-20 00:07] decide — first land workspace scaffolding and package facades so later relocation can happen incrementally.
 >>[2026-03-20 00:07] taste — prefer one compatibility layer per package over a half-moved tree with unstable imports.
 >>[2026-03-20 00:11] decide — scope the initial workspace to packages/* plus extensions/vscode-spw, because IntelliJ is not an npm workspace surface.
 >>[2026-03-20 00:11] revise — root exports now point at package facades for seed/runtime while scripts remain on current paths.
 >>[2026-03-20 00:11] decide — CLI gets a real facade over scripts/spw-cli, while LSP stays a truthful scaffold constant until executable extraction is ready.
 >>[2026-03-20 00:14] observe — root runtime tests still fail on Substrate.bind expectations, which appears pre-existing and outside this workspace scaffold slice.
 >>[2026-03-20 00:15] observe — direct smoke imports for all new package facades succeed, so the new seams are loadable even though root build/test still carry unrelated pre-existing failures.
}

